From 9b0e19d45f30258448300e5a33cb9417eaad8e82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xjc10 <69450118+xjc10@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 00:54:06 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] DP prompt path on 2x RX 6900 XT: on-demand DP beside --batch
 slots, staged foreign rows, drafter catch-up (all opt-in)

- WeightTable::find: the DP fallback looks only at the other table's own rows (a name neither holds recursed until SIGSEGV)
- STRATA_DP_BATCH=1: the DP start gate with --batch slots; the STRATA_PIPED_CONCURRENT read steps aside when the DP path takes the read
- STRATA_DP_LAZY=1: the DP foreign sessions are laid out in the slots a DP read borrows (Prefill::set_dp_room), not held in VRAM
- STRATA_DP_STAGE_W=N / STRATA_DP_STAGE_MIN=<bytes>: a ring of N per-layer slots the stage-trimmed peer's rows of a foreign layer are copied into (rows below MIN stay in place; 0 copies every row)
- STRATA_DP_MTP_ALL=1: both paths' chunks reach the drafter in prompt order
- STRATA_DP_STAGE_TIMING=1 / STRATA_DP_TRACE=1: diagnostics
- STRATA_DP_MTP_ALL etc. measured in notes E663-E676

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
